00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:06.309 align:start position:0%
the hayate hotel in mogadishu turned  into a battleground on friday night  al-shabab gunmen blasted their way into  the building  with two car bombs before seizing  control of it  somali security forces launched a  counter-offensive witnesses say there  were several explosions followed by  exchanges of gunfire that continued  through the night and into saturday  al-shabab has claimed responsibility  these types of attacks have been a  hallmark of ultraviolet operations a  couple years ago in particular and they  kind of slowed down a little bit but we  see them popping up again  footage from the scene shows extensive  damage to the hotel  several people have been taken to  hospital  the victims reportedly include children  as well as the hotel's owner these  hotels are usually attacked because  that's areas where government officials  congregate  and so there's a lot of meetings a lot  of activity especially right now with  the new government coming into into  place and setting up a lot of its  appointments and its positions but  there's also  often been a secondary element to some  of these you know al-shabab runs a very  extensive extortion racket within  mogadishu itself and they've targeted  business owners that haven't complied as  well  the armed group is affiliated to  al-qaeda and has carried numerous  attacks in mogadishu in the past decade  its aim is to establish a system of  government in somalia based on sharia  law muhammad al jazeera
 

